Driver/GT10Audio.c	undated	OSStatus four-char codes such as '!obj' are positive, so returning one as a HRESULT passes SUCCEEDED(). Apple's own NullAudio sample does this. Only E_* values may leave QueryInterface.
Driver/GT10Audio.c	undated	StartStream must register the stream request even when the pedal is absent. The device stays listed while unplugged, so an app can start recording first. Returning early leaves wantStream false, and the monitor then never starts a stream when the pedal arrives: the app records silence until it stops and starts IO again.
Driver/GT10Audio.c	undated	The HAL clock is one atomic word (seed << 2 | source: stopped, synthetic, device) changed only by CAS, because a separate streaming flag and seed raced removal against StartIO's commit. The device clock is committed on the monitor queue after the first captured timestamp. IO admission (count in, then read the clock) plus the owner's prepare step on the monitor queue is what makes the ring reset safe. Codex GO after three review rounds, 2026-09-17.
Driver/GT10Audio.c	undated	The IO path must reject a sample position that does not belong to the ring it addresses. The clock word can flip between the HAL fetching a cycle's timestamp and that cycle reaching ReadInput, so one cycle carries a synthetic position into the device ring. The reader's floor only rises and the writer's end only moves forward, so a single stray position silences the device for the rest of the session. Found by review 2026-09-20, guarded by PositionOnTimeline.
