Driver/GT10USBDevice.cpp	undated	A faulted stream must be started again by the monitor. The HAL never repeats StartIO, so without a restart one late transfer leaves the device alive, running and silent until the app or the cable moves. Bounded to kMaxFaultRestarts per stream request so a dead device cannot spin.
Driver/GT10USBDevice.cpp	undated	A monitor that ever quarantined a stream (abandoned stop, stop timeout, unconfirmed alt 0) is never freed and never streams again, because an abandoned engine thread can still call back into it through faultContext.
Driver/GT10USBDevice.cpp	undated	Acquisition gives up after 5 attempts over about 3 seconds and then waits for an arrival notification. A coreaudiod restart outlives that window: the previous plug-in host still holds the interfaces and the pedal never moves, so no arrival ever comes and the device stays published and dead. Hit on hardware 2026-09-20. GT10USBMonitorSetStream now also tries to acquire when a client asks for audio.
Driver/GT10USBDevice.cpp	undated	An unplug faults the engine before the termination notification arrives, because transfers fail first. So a failed alt 0 restore must NOT be permanent: it belongs to the attachment and is cleared when the device is released. Only an engine that could not be joined quarantines for the life of the process. Verified by an unplug and replug on hardware 2026-09-18: without the split the driver held the pedal but never streamed again.
